# the way in, remembered: the tool ids you passed through to reach the tool
# that is open, oldest first. Navigation is per-instance and never travels, so
# device-scoped exactly as /tools' own open_tool is — and a device write queues
# no op. Not bridged: nothing on the page half reads it, and a bridged key
# written from a link newer than /payload paints a stale frame.
parents: String = "[]".to_string() (device, last-write, own)
